Yes, the "pick a setting" dropdown was standing in for the search bar that's already in the left nav. The plan doesn't add a second search to the node page.

To be clear about what the prototype did: a jump didn't collapse anything, it only opened the target section. You may have seen headers collapsed because I'd asked you to click Collapse all first. Your rule is stricter than that, and I've written it into [the plan](.claude/plans/eng-2409-plan.md):

- **Search jump:** resets the node page to all sections expanded, scrolls to the setting and flashes it. It never collapses anything.
- **Side effect:** the jump also undoes any sections you had collapsed earlier in that dialog session, because collapse state is shared across node types. Your "all expanded" wording implies that's what you want; tell me if you'd rather keep your other collapses.
- **Content hints:** removed, along with the search catalog change they needed. Collapsed headers show only the section name.

The plan now covers:
- collapsible sections on the node page, all expanded by default, with Collapse/Expand all in the fixed breadcrumb header;
- sticky section headers on every settings page that has them;
- clicking a stuck header collapses that section and keeps its header in place;
- collapse state lasts for the dialog's lifetime and is shared across node types;
- the search jump behaviour above.

No other decisions are open. Should I treat this as approved? If so, I'll save it to the session context as the approved plan and start implementing.

